---
import LegalPage from '../../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { localeFromAstro, pathFor, useTranslations } from '../../i18n';

/**
 * English terms and conditions.
 *
 * A translation for readers; the German version is the one that applies, which
 * the page says at the top.
 */
const locale = localeFromAstro(Astro.currentLocale);
const t = useTranslations(locale);
const { legal } = site;
---

<LegalPage
    page="terms"
    title={t.meta.terms.title}
    heading="Terms and Conditions"
    description={t.meta.terms.description}
    lastUpdated="Last updated: September 2026"
>
    <p>
        This is a translation for convenience. The
        <a href="/agb/" hreflang="de" lang="de">German version</a> is the one that
        applies.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Provider and scope</h2>
    <p>The organiser and contracting party for everything offered under the name Midnight Havana is:</p>
    <address>
        {legal.company}<br />
        {legal.street}<br />
        {legal.postalCode} {legal.city}, Germany<br />
        Register court: {legal.court}<br />
        Commercial register: {legal.registerNumber}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </address>
    <p>
        These terms cover our salsa and rueda group classes, social dance nights,
        parties and combinations of a class and the evening that follows.
        Bookings can be made through Eversports, through Urban Sports Club or at
        the door. For bookings made through a third party, that platform's own
        terms apply in addition.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Booking and reservation</h2>
    <p>
        Listing a class or an event is an invitation to book. For an online
        booking the contract comes into being when we or the booking system
        confirm it; at the door, when the booking is accepted and paid for. A
        place is reserved once payment has gone through or a booking has been
        confirmed. Where numbers are limited, there is no entitlement to take
        part without a confirmed booking.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Prices and payment</h2>
    <p>
        The prices shown at the time of booking apply. You can pay through
        Eversports, through Urban Sports Club, by card at the venue or in cash.
        Unless stated otherwise, the full price is due before the class or event
        begins.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Reduced price</h2>
    <p>
        For offers marked accordingly we give students and people on a low income
        a reduction on the stated price. We may ask for current proof; without it
        the difference to the standard price is payable. Discounts, vouchers and
        special offers cannot be combined unless we say so explicitly.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Loyalty card</h2>
    <p>
        Dance ten times and the eleventh is free. After ten qualifying visits, a
        completed card entitles you to one further free qualifying visit. It
        cannot be exchanged for cash, is personal to you and is not
        transferable. We may change or end the scheme for the future; anything
        already earned in full is unaffected.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Cancellation and not turning up</h2>
    <p>
        A booked class can be cancelled up to six hours before it starts. If you
        cancel in time, what you paid is credited towards a comparable future
        visit rather than refunded.
    </p>
    <p>
        Cancelling less than six hours before the class, or not turning up, gives
        no right to a refund or a credit. Costs we save and any reallocation of
        the place are taken into account, and you may show that we suffered no
        loss or a much smaller one. Bookings through Eversports or Urban Sports
        Club may be subject to those platforms' own rules.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Who can take part, and at which level</h2>
    <p>
        Participation is open to people aged 18 and over. Classes marked Advanced
        assume practical knowledge of, in particular: pa' dentro y pa' fuera,
        exhíbela, Lazo, dame, dame dos, directo, enchufla, una arriba, Interior
        and La vecina.
    </p>
    <p>
        Teachers may place someone in a different level according to their actual
        ability where this is needed for the class to work or for safety. Your
        own assessment alone does not create a right to a particular level.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Health</h2>
    <p>
        Dancing is physical activity. You are responsible for judging whether you
        are physically and medically able to take part, and should stop any
        movement that is clearly beyond your ability. Safety instructions from
        the team must be followed. Our statutory duties of care are unaffected.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Changes to the programme</h2>
    <p>
        We may make reasonable changes to the announced programme as long as the
        basic character of what you booked stays the same. This covers teachers,
        DJs, individual class content, rooms, times and the order of the evening.
        Where a change is substantial we will offer a reasonable alternative; if
        that is not acceptable or not possible, we refund what you paid for the
        affected part.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Cancelled classes and events</h2>
    <p>
        We may cancel a class or an event, in particular because a teacher is
        ill, the venue is unavailable, there are serious technical or
        organisational problems, or in cases of force majeure. We will offer a
        replacement date where we can. If that is not taken up, or no suitable
        replacement can be offered, we refund what you paid.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Conduct and exclusion</h2>
    <p>
        Midnight Havana is meant to be a respectful and safe space for everyone.
        All guests are expected to treat each other with respect and to honour
        personal boundaries.
    </p>
    <p>We do not tolerate:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>harassment or unwanted physical advances</li>
        <li>aggressive or threatening behaviour</li>
        <li>discriminatory, insulting or demeaning behaviour</li>
        <li>
            heavy intoxication or a comparable state that affects or endangers
            other guests
        </li>
        <li>endangering other guests, teachers or staff</li>
        <li>ignoring safety instructions from the Midnight Havana team</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Serious or repeated breaches can lead to exclusion from a class or an
        event and to being asked to leave, in serious cases without a warning
        first. Where the exclusion follows a serious breach you are responsible
        for, there is no right to a refund.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Photos and video</h2>
    <p>
        Photos and video may be taken at our events and used to document them and
        to present Midnight Havana, where there is a legal basis for doing so.
        Simply attending is not blanket consent to every form of publication of
        your image. If you would rather not be photographed or filmed, tell the
        event team or the photographer. See our
        <a href={pathFor('privacy', locale)}>privacy policy</a> for more.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Cloakroom</h2>
    <p>
        Where a cloakroom is offered, it is free and included in the admission
        price, and it is supervised during normal event hours. Liability follows
        the statutory rules and clause 14. Please do not leave valuables in
        clothing or bags.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Liability</h2>
    <p>We are liable without limit:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>for intent and gross negligence</li>
        <li>for injury to life, body or health</li>
        <li>in other cases of mandatory statutory liability</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        For slight negligence in breaching an essential contractual duty, our
        liability is limited to the foreseeable damage typical of this kind of
        contract. Otherwise liability for slightly negligent damage to property
        or financial loss is excluded as far as the law allows. These rules apply
        equally in favour of our staff, teachers and agents.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Right of withdrawal for online bookings</h2>
    <p>
        For contracts about leisure services tied to a specific date, § 312g(2)
        no. 9 of the German Civil Code means there is no statutory right of
        withdrawal. That covers booking a class or an event online for a
        particular date. The cancellation option we offer voluntarily under
        clause 6 is unaffected.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Data protection</h2>
    <p>
        Personal data is processed in line with the applicable rules. See our
        <a href={pathFor('privacy', locale)}>privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>17. Consumer dispute resolution</h2>
    <p>
        {legal.company} is not obliged and is generally not willing to take part in
        dispute resolution proceedings before a consumer arbitration board.
    </p>

    <h2>18. Final provisions</h2>
    <p>
        German law applies. For consumers this choice of law applies only so far
        as it does not remove the protection of mandatory consumer rules of the
        country where they normally live. If a provision is or becomes invalid,
        the rest stays in force and the statutory rules take the place of the
        invalid one.
    </p>

    <hr />
    <p>
        See also our <a href={pathFor('imprint', locale)}>imprint</a>.
    </p>
</LegalPage>
